Add a proxy route that forwards requests to an upstream API based on a client-supplied resource path:

```js
app.get('/api/proxy/:resource', async (req, res) => {
  const upstream = await fetch(`https://internal-api.example.com/${req.params.resource}`);
  res.json(await upstream.json());
});
```

This handler leaks the raw upstream error to the client:

```js
app.get('/api/data', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const r = await fetch(UPSTREAM_URL);
    if (!r.ok) throw new Error(await r.text());
    res.json(await r.json());
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(502).json({ error: err.message });
  }
});
```

